WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.625 --> 00:00:20.289
"Wow!" exclaimed.

2
00:00:20.309 --> 00:00:22.590
"First City is huge!"

3
00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:27.351
Zann hadn't been back to the capital since he and Boz had moved to Swamp Bottom.

4
00:00:27.991 --> 00:00:31.152
He leaned forward, searching for a glimpse of his old neighborhood.

5
00:00:31.788 --> 00:00:35.670
But it was hard to get his bearings from way up in the sky, and before he knew

6
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:38.232
it, the dragons were circling lower and lower.

7
00:00:39.353 --> 00:00:41.334
They landed in a clearing outside of town.

8
00:00:41.354 --> 00:00:45.236
"This looks like a safe spot for the dragons to rest," Darb said.

9
00:00:46.036 --> 00:00:48.278
Zann's legs felt stiff as he jumped down.

10
00:00:48.958 --> 00:00:53.821
The dragons had flown swiftly, but it had taken almost two hours to reach their destination.

11
00:00:53.841 --> 00:00:55.302
"Now what?"

12
00:00:55.662 --> 00:00:56.222
Gliss asked.

13
00:00:56.242 --> 00:00:58.684
"Does anyone know how to get to the palace?"

14
00:00:59.784 --> 00:01:03.848
Zann reached into his pocket, checking to make sure Boz's diary was still there.

15
00:01:03.868 --> 00:01:07.471
"I remember my way around well enough," he said.

16
00:01:07.491 --> 00:01:08.431
"I'll find it."

17
00:01:10.393 --> 00:01:11.474
They hiked through the woods.

18
00:01:12.094 --> 00:01:16.818
As soon as Zann saw the ramshackle buildings at the city limits, he realized where they were.

19
00:01:16.838 --> 00:01:20.481
"This area is called Wormwood," he told the others.

20
00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.264
"It's not the best part of town."

21
00:01:23.284 --> 00:01:26.567
"Really?" Gliss said nervously.

22
00:01:26.587 --> 00:01:28.048
"What's wrong with it?"

23
00:01:28.848 --> 00:01:35.251
"Everyone says it got its name because there's a wormhole near some gnarled old tree here," Zann explained.

24
00:01:35.271 --> 00:01:40.113
"And that the locals figured out how to use it to bring stuff back from other worlds."

25
00:01:41.073 --> 00:01:42.794
"I've read about that," Darb said.

26
00:01:42.814 --> 00:01:48.577
"People say there's a thriving black market here for exotic otherworld pets and stuff."

27
00:01:48.597 --> 00:01:52.538
"Sounds cool, but let's remember why we're here, okay?"

28
00:01:52.918 --> 00:01:53.439
said Perda.

29
00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:56.320
"We need to get that diary to the palace."

30
00:01:58.632 --> 00:01:59.813
Zann knew she was right.

31
00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:04.136
Still, he couldn't help watching for the notorious tree as he walked.

32
00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:05.477
"Is that it?"

33
00:02:05.697 --> 00:02:06.377
Darb pointed.

34
00:02:07.398 --> 00:02:13.062
Just ahead was a tree so ancient and twisted that it appeared to be carved out of stone.

35
00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:18.906
Several huts stood near its massive trunk, their entrances obscured by draped fabric.

36
00:02:19.666 --> 00:02:24.049
An old woman was in front of one of the huts, stirring something in a brass pot.

37
00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.032
She stared at Zann and Gliss with dark, sunken eyes.

38
00:02:29.036 --> 00:02:34.260
"Beware, my young Red friends," she said, her voice coarse and deep.

39
00:02:35.041 --> 00:02:38.704
"There are trolls all over town looking for your kind."

40
00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.466
"Oh no!"

41
00:02:40.946 --> 00:02:41.727
Gliss squeaked.

42
00:02:41.747 --> 00:02:43.148
"What if they see us?"

43
00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.290
"I can help," the woman said.

44
00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:51.334
"I have scarves to cover your hair and a paste to hide your freckles."

45
00:02:52.355 --> 00:02:54.277
"Really?" Gliss sounded relieved.

46
00:02:54.297 --> 00:02:55.438
"Thank you!"

47
00:02:55.458 --> 00:02:57.680
"Not so fast."

48
00:02:58.248 --> 00:02:59.508
The woman held up a hand.

49
00:02:59.528 --> 00:03:05.010
"I am just a poor merchant and cannot afford to give away my wares.

50
00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.931
What do you have to offer me in trade?"

51
00:03:07.951 --> 00:03:10.651
"Trade?" Zann was confused.

52
00:03:11.352 --> 00:03:16.653
Since most people used magic for their daily needs, trading was uncommon except among Voids.

53
00:03:16.673 --> 00:03:19.554
"We have nothing of value," Darb said.

54
00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:22.635
"Perhaps we can pay you for the disguises later."

55
00:03:23.935 --> 00:03:25.275
"Nothing of value?"

56
00:03:25.676 --> 00:03:27.720
The woman had spotted Zing.

57
00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.681
"The fire whistler—is it yours?"

58
00:03:30.522 --> 00:03:31.862
"Yes," Zann said.

59
00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:34.484
"But he's not for trade at any price!"

60
00:03:34.504 --> 00:03:35.885
"A shame."

61
00:03:36.345 --> 00:03:37.826
Her eyes lingered on the dragon.

62
00:03:37.846 --> 00:03:40.427
"Then I'm afraid I cannot help you."

63
00:03:41.168 --> 00:03:43.089
"Please!" Perda stepped forward.

64
00:03:43.109 --> 00:03:49.393
"If you only knew why we've come here, you'd—" "Never mind," Zann interrupted quickly.

65
00:03:50.073 --> 00:03:54.375
Even though the woman had warned them about the trolls, there was something about her that Zann didn't

66
00:03:54.455 --> 00:03:55.196
quite trust.

67
00:03:55.944 --> 00:03:58.545
"We'll figure out another way to disguise ourselves."

68
00:03:59.345 --> 00:04:00.306
The old woman shrugged.

69
00:04:00.326 --> 00:04:01.847
"Good luck to you then."

70
00:04:02.947 --> 00:04:04.728
She turned her attention back to her pot.

71
00:04:05.668 --> 00:04:09.049
Darb and the girls were already moving on, but Zann hesitated.

72
00:04:09.069 --> 00:04:10.690
"So is it true?"

73
00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:11.851
he asked the woman.

74
00:04:11.871 --> 00:04:13.972
"About the wormhole, I mean.

75
00:04:14.772 --> 00:04:17.933
Is there really a passage to other worlds near this tree?"

76
00:04:17.953 --> 00:04:21.835
"I have no idea what you're talking about," she replied.

77
00:04:21.855 --> 00:04:24.396
"Though I could try to find out.

78
00:04:25.592 --> 00:04:26.913
For a price, of course."

79
00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:33.437
Zann frowned, suddenly certain that she knew much more about the wormhole than she was admitting.

80
00:04:33.457 --> 00:04:40.022
"I'd ask my parents," he blurted out angrily, "but they disappeared through a wormhole much like this one

81
00:04:40.102 --> 00:04:41.082
four years ago!"

82
00:04:41.963 --> 00:04:44.625
He bit his lip, wishing he hadn't said that out loud.

83
00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:49.988
Now the woman was studying his face curiously, a hint of recognition in her eyes.

84
00:04:50.909 --> 00:04:52.290
Or was that his imagination?

85
00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:54.932
"Wait here," she commanded.

86
00:04:55.284 --> 00:04:56.565
She disappeared into her hut.

87
00:04:57.305 --> 00:05:02.468
Soon she was back, pressing a wad of fabric and a small glass vial into Zann's hands.

88
00:05:02.488 --> 00:05:04.689
"Take these," she said.

89
00:05:04.709 --> 00:05:08.611
"It's my gift to you as as a visitor to Wormwood."

90
00:05:09.511 --> 00:05:12.853
She handed the items to Zann and then went back to stirring her pot.

91
00:05:12.873 --> 00:05:15.054
"Zann?" Perda called.

92
00:05:15.074 --> 00:05:16.274
"What are you doing?"

93
00:05:16.294 --> 00:05:19.256
"That woman just gave me these."

94
00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:25.512
He hurried over to his friends and unfurled a couple of long, gauzy scarves while Gliss grabbed the

95
00:05:25.552 --> 00:05:26.633
vial and examined it.

96
00:05:26.653 --> 00:05:28.794
"It's the disguise stuff!"

97
00:05:29.254 --> 00:05:29.815
she exclaimed.

98
00:05:29.835 --> 00:05:31.996
"Why'd the woman change her mind?"

99
00:05:32.016 --> 00:05:35.659
"Who knows, but I'm glad she did," Perda said.

100
00:05:35.679 --> 00:05:37.940
"I'll help you with your scarf, Zann."

101
00:05:38.961 --> 00:05:43.584
While Perda fussed with Zann's hair, Gliss covered her freckles with the liquid from the vial.

102
00:05:44.225 --> 00:05:47.147
The whole time Zann couldn't help staring at the woman.

103
00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:52.222
What had it meant, that glimmer of recognition he'd seen after mentioning his parents?

104
00:05:52.982 --> 00:05:55.644
Could she possibly know something about what had happened to them?

105
00:05:55.664 --> 00:05:58.666
"There!" Perda finished Zann's disguise.

106
00:05:58.686 --> 00:06:01.007
"Now nobody will know you're a Red."

107
00:06:02.008 --> 00:06:02.708
"How do I look?"

108
00:06:03.068 --> 00:06:03.629
Gliss asked.

109
00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:05.470
Zann barely heard them.

110
00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.392
He wanted to walk over and demand to know what the woman knew.

111
00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.374
But no matter how much he wanted to do that, he knew he couldn't.

112
00:06:13.915 --> 00:06:14.515
Not right now.

113
00:06:15.756 --> 00:06:19.526
Boz, his friends, and possibly all of Magica were relying on him.

114
00:06:19.546 --> 00:06:21.912
"Let's get moving," he said.
